EXT. PAWS AND PEACE PET CREMATORIUM DRIVE-THRU - DAY

A cheerful pastel kiosk with a speaker box and a pull-up window. WALLY PRUITT, fifties, in a polo shirt with a paw-print logo, sits inside with a headset on. KIKI NAKAMURA, twenties, his new trainee, stands behind him holding a clipboard.

He taps the headset. She leans in to watch.

                    WALLY
          Okay, Kiki, first rule. We never say "dead."

                    KIKI
          What do we say?

                    WALLY
          "Passed on to the big yard."

She writes it down. He presses a button.

                    WALLY (CONT'D)
          Welcome to Paws and Peace. How can we comfort you today?

The speaker crackles.

                    DESMOND (V.O.)
          Yeah, hi. I got a pet. It's, uh, in the car. Back seat.

                    WALLY
          I'm so sorry for your loss, sir. May I ask what kind of companion?

                    DESMOND (V.O.)
          A python. Eleven feet.

He freezes. She stops writing. They look at each other.

                    KIKI
          Wally, is that a big yard thing?

                    WALLY
          Hush. (into mic) Sir, ah, our standard urn holds up to eighty pounds.

                    DESMOND (V.O.)
          He's got a roommate. She's pretty upset.

                    WALLY
          The, uh, the family is grieving?

                    DESMOND (V.O.)
          No. The other python. She's in the car too.

Kiki drops the clipboard. He waves a hand at her to stay calm, then peers through the window at a dusty hatchback idling in the lane.

The hatchback's rear window is a solid wall of coiled scales.

                    KIKI
          Wally, the glass is moving.

                    WALLY
          Don't say "moving."

                    DESMOND (V.O.)
          Hey, Wally, right? Your tag says Wally. Can you make the window go up? I think she's trying to hug the heater.

He rips off the headset and stands. She backs toward the door.

                    WALLY
          Kiki. Kiki! Be a pro. Tell him we will be right out.

                    KIKI
          You tell him!

                    WALLY
          I am training YOU!

The speaker crackles again.

                    DESMOND (V.O.)
          Is this a bad time? I can come back.

Wally and Kiki both shout "No!" at the same moment, then stare at each other, appalled.
